<!--
  The USB devices the appliance is offered for: the serial bridges RNode hardware
  presents, by the vendor and product each one reports.

  Android reads these as decimal numbers, and it matches the device the radio
  reports rather than the interface, so an entry is a vendor and a product and
  nothing else. An entry with no attributes is not a filter but every USB device
  there is, which is why none of them is written that way.

  The radio on the tablet this was written for is the first entry: an Espressif USB
  JTAG/serial debug unit, which is the ESP32-S3's own USB port and what a Heltec v4
  RNode presents. The three below it are the bridge chips RNode boards ship with.
-->
<resources>
    <!-- Espressif USB JTAG/serial debug unit (ESP32-S3 native USB): 0x303a:0x1001 -->
    <usb-device vendor-id="12346" product-id="4097" />

    <!-- Silicon Labs CP2102: 0x10c4:0xea60 -->
    <usb-device vendor-id="4292" product-id="60000" />

    <!-- QinHeng CH340: 0x1a86:0x7523 -->
    <usb-device vendor-id="6790" product-id="29987" />

    <!-- FTDI FT232R: 0x0403:0x6001 -->
    <usb-device vendor-id="1027" product-id="24577" />
</resources>
